description:
FILED s536a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from #135 (Role-Tiny concrete-methods.t *FILE*: "Undefined subroutine &MyRole1::before_constant_deflate").  PRE-EXISTING on main 06a4b8ba (code sha); s522b measured half (1) and wrote it into #135.

REPRODUCERS (scratch/s536a/p/135-10.pl, 135-12.pl in the s536a worktree):

    BEGIN {
      use constant X1 => 1;
      print "a: ", X1, "\n";
    }
    BEGIN {
      package R;
      use constant X2 => 2;
      print "b: ", X2, "\n";
    }
    print "c: ", R::X2(), "\n";
    sub f { package R4; use constant X4 => 4; return X4; }
    print "d: ", f(), " ", R4::X4(), "\n";

perl 5.40.3: `a: 1` / `b: 2` / `c: 2` / `d: 4 4`.
PCL: `a: X1` / `b: X2` / dies "Undefined subroutine &R::X2 called" (and &R4::X4 for the sub form).

TWO bugs:
(1) QUALIFICATION -- Pl/Parser.pm _emit_constant names the sub with `_qualified_sub_to_cl($name)` alone, so `use constant` after a `package R;` INSIDE a block (a BEGIN, a sub; the seam passes block_depth 1) emits `(p-sub pl-X2 ...)`, read in the SECTION's package (main): R::X2 is never defined.  v1's named-sub path (Parser.pm ~7354, `_block_depth > 0` => "$pkg::$name") and Parser2's _sub_name_for_emission qualify; this sibling does not.  A bare block `{ package S; use constant SC => 7 }` at file level works (the section switches).  Fix: one shared helper for the in-block qualification (rule 11) used by _emit_constant (both arms: p-use-constant and p-sub).
(2) RECOGNITION -- a bareword naming a constant declared by a `use constant` EARLIER IN THE SAME BEGIN block is a STRING ("X1"), even with no package switch; the #2610 detector table records the call as "unknown".  A constant from an EARLIER BEGIN, or in a bare block, is recognised.  Not located: the #711 pre-pass registers it (_premerge_use_constant_prototypes, site = the use statement); the BEGIN is lowered by v1 through the seam (kind `scheduled`), so the question is which prototype lookup / site the seam's v1 parse of the BEGIN body consults.
ROWS: Role-Tiny-2.002004-0 concrete-methods.t *FILE* -- re-keyed from #135 by s536a; the file has more after these two (stubs = #4561, `$MyRole1::{blorf} = sub {...}` a stash element write = the deferred live-stash model, constants' stash representation), so fixing this moves the file's stop, not necessarily its verdict.
